# Implementation phases

> Purpose: build in five ordered phases, one function at a time. Track status in Profile → **Current phase** (`P1`…`P5` \| `done`). Never mix phases; finish the exit gate first.

| Phase | Name | Focus |
|-------|------|--------|
| **P1** | Foundation | Concept lock, design + layout approved, tokens, skeleton, migrations (+ seeds) |
| **P2** | Mock UI + mock data | Every route built to `route-layouts.mdc` on mock adapters — no real API |
| **P3** | API backend | Real API on applied schema, endpoint by endpoint — UI stays on mocks |
| **P4** | Integration | Wire UI → API feature by feature; remove/replace mocks |
| **P5** | Cleanup & ship | Dead code, docs, regression, security/perf pass, deploy checklist |

## How detail works (specific, function by function)

During install (after concept + routes are known) the AI writes the concrete plan into **`phase-plan.mdc`** (`format.mdc` ID scheme: `F` → `R`/`E`/`T` → `U`). Sub-tasks below are the *generic skeleton*; `phase-plan.mdc` is the *project-specific* list.

### Rule of specificity

1. **One function/unit = one `U-nn` line item** with a Function Spec (template below). No "implement auth" — instead `AuthService.login()`, `AuthService.refresh()`, `requireRole()`, `LoginForm.onSubmit()`, …
2. **Order inside a phase:** dependencies first (types/contracts → helpers → core functions → composition → tests).
3. **Every line item has a Definition of Done** the AI can check (file exists, function signature matches spec, test passes, states covered).
4. **Status per item:** `todo` → `doing` → `done` \| `deferred (reason)` (`format.mdc`). Update in `phase-plan.mdc` as work happens.
5. Work **one item at a time**; do not start an item whose dependencies are not `done`.
6. Any new function discovered mid-phase is **added to the plan first**, then built.

### Function Spec (copy per function / unit)

```
#### <Module.function or Component> — <one-line purpose>
- ID / phase / feature: <U-nn> · <P#> · <F-nn> (+ R/E/T ids)
- File: <path>
- Depends on: <other items / contracts / tables>
- Input: <params + types + validation rules>
- Output: <return type / response shape (success)>
- Errors: <error cases → code/message/field mapping>
- Authz: <role/ownership check, or "public">
- Side effects: <db writes, events, cache, files>
- UI states (if UI): <loading skeleton · empty · error · success>
- Layout (if UI): <route block in route-layouts.mdc + mobile/tablet/desktop notes>
- Components:   <catalog components + variants used (ui-components.mdc)>
- Overrides:    <Component → className / classNames.slot → why, or none (ui-components.mdc §1b)>
- Tests: <cases: happy · validation fail · authz fail · edge>
- Done when: <checkable criteria>
- Status: todo
```

